					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anqxyr" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(966960); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=966960&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1610119011" alt="anqxyr" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=966960)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/anqxyr" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(966960); return false;" >anqxyr</a></span> <span class="odate time_1321810486 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">20 Nov 2011 17:34</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1310499">
									

<p>From &quot;How To Write An SCP&quot; guide:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>a thing that will liquefy bone in a quarter-mile radius is very dangerous, and would need special containment, but it’s not interesting.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is too close to that for me to upvote.</p>
<p>However, writing and tone are unusually good for a first-try SCP, so I can't downvote it either. My only nitpick is a little too heavy use of expungement. For example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is difficult to determine the precise date &#8230; effects first began at or around █ February, 19██.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Knowing the date is pretty precise. You can just say &quot;around February, 19██&quot;, or drop the &quot;difficult to determine&quot; part and state exact date. Also, I hate 19██-like dates and would suggest that you just pick a date instead of blackboxing it, but that's mostly my personal reaction and other people may not agree with me on this.</p>
<p>Another example:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>involving a case of necrotizing [REDACTED].</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Again, just pick a disease that causes necrosis and use it instead of [REDACTED]. Also, my spellchecker says that necrotizing isn't a word, but he says many things and I don't usually trust him.</p>
<p>And again, from the table:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Between █ and ██ hours of exposure [DATA EXPUNGED]</p>
</blockquote>
<p>If you have a whole section with the only content been [DATA EXPUNGED], you have a problem with expungement.</p>
<p>And yet again:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The [REDACTED] Project</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Just pick a name and stick with it. On average, the less expungements article has, the stronger effect and meaning each of them have.</p>
<p>I don't know how to vote on this. Writing is mostly good, but concept is bland. I don't like to no-vote articles, but I just may have to in this case, unless you somehow expand the idea into something more interesting, so that I can upvote without feeling guilty.</p>

							</div>

								
