			<div class="content" id="post-content-1310521">
									

<p>Hi. Thanks for feedback.</p>
<p>To be completely honest, I couldn't really think of anything all that disgusting when I hit a certain point in designing the chart, so I just expunged some of the data and left it at that. I thought that maybe someone else's imagination could think up a more horrifying sequence of events to plug the gaps, preferably involving blowfly larvae and gangrene. Maybe I will elaborate a little&#8230;</p>
<p>Same thing with the project name. Of course, maybe it's just secret enough that hiding what it's called is required, but the Foundation isn't particularly concerned with low-level employees knowing that they've got someone working on the thing. If I ever think up a good name, I'll change that.</p>
<p>For the disease: I was thinking of necrotizing fasciitis when I was writing the cover story. Didn't want to go and say it outright, so I redacted that part. According to Wikipedia, Herod the Great may have had the thing in his groin regions. Isn't that a lovely way to die.</p>
<p>I see what you mean about the specific date. I will edit that ASAP.</p>
<p>If there's really a large amount of demand for it, I may add an interview log or something with young Sally ██████ and have her tell the doctor/embedded agent about how she wants her arm to be whole again. I'm not sure how it'll turn out, so unless loads of people really want to see me try I won't do it yet.</p>
<p>I'll argue that the item is a little more detailed than a simple &quot;oh god it kills you in horrible ways&quot; but that's really up to opinion.</p>

