<blockquote>
<p>how she wants her arm to be whole again.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>And this pushed me to upvote. Now you need to make so that mental image I just had would be more visible from the description. No idea how you do that. Interview may improve the article and may make it worse, depending on how well you'll pull it off.</p>
<p>Maybe you should also increase the timespan, to, say, two-three month, with necrosis slowly propagating through skin and muscle tissue, but without affecting organs until later stage, so that Sally and her parents will have more time to savor the effects. You can have different time intervals for &quot;subject was wearing the mitten too long, effect is now irreversible&quot; and &quot;necrosis is fully manifested, subject will die soon&quot;. 24-hours seems alright for the first one. Also, subjects in later stages, when muscle tissue is already gone, but organs don't affected for couple of weeks yet, may die from starvation if they live alone and no one else knows that something is happening to them.</p>
<p>So, yes, you have a room for improvement, use it.</p>

